// A module declaring both kinds of **templates**, for the imports corpus to distinguish.
//
// ADR-0230 permits imported pure `$T` procedures, while imported `$N` procedures remain E0268 because their
// compile-time values require a separate cross-file const-eval dependency. `imports/invalid/017` pins that
// narrower refusal through `scaled`.
//
// The wrapper remains as historical and composition coverage: `imports/valid/017` proves an owner-local
// specialization can still sit behind an ordinary imported procedure.

/// A pure `$T` template. ADR-0230 permits importing and specializing this shape.
identity :: (x: $T) -> T {
  return x;
}

/// A `$N` comptime-value template. Instantiating this from another file remains E0268.
scaled :: ($N: s64, factor: s64) -> s64 {
  return N * factor;
}

/// An owner-local specialization exposed through an ordinary procedure.
identity_int :: (x: s64) -> s64 {
  return identity(x);
}
